# Repo-root line-ending rules.
#
# `cutdown/.gitattributes` covers `cutdown/**` only, which left the GENERATED skill
# mirror uncovered: it lives at `.claude/skills/cutdown-*/SKILL.md`, above the cutdown
# workspace. With `core.autocrlf=true` those files would still arrive CRLF on a fresh
# clone, and `cutdown skills sync` decides both ownership (the generated banner anchor)
# and staleness (`--check`) by comparing text — so every mirror would be misclassified
# as hand-written and `--check` would be permanently stale on a tree nobody touched.
#
# `normaliseNewlines` in `apps/cli/src/commands/skills-sync.ts` also defends both
# comparisons. For files under `cutdown/`, that is a fallback for checkouts predating
# the attributes file. For the mirror, it was the ONLY protection until this file
# existed.
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed on a Linux host. Under core.autocrlf=true a CRLF
# checkout turns every backslash line continuation into an escaped carriage
# return, so `pg_dump --dbname=... \` + CRLF runs as `pg_dump ... r` and the
# next line as a command. Measured 2026-09-07: 10 broken continuations in
# scripts/backup.sh and 6 in scripts/restore-drill.sh, reproduced with
# `git checkout-index` through the real filters. The working tree being LF is
# NOT the fix -- the blob was already LF; the checkout filter is what breaks it.
*.sh    text eol=lf
